# §3.2.2
c(75, "§3.2.2 Simplicity and design — the specific repeated instruction: do not add anything; 'Please don't try to be an all in one app!'; 'without bloat. Plz keep it that way'; 'Keine Pflanze, die mitwächst, kein Timer, den man nicht benutzt'; 'no gamification overload, no feeling that managing the habit tracker becomes a habit in itself'", "product-rule",
  "'Add nothing' is a user-stated product requirement, stated more often and more emphatically than any single feature request: 'Please do not add any unnecessary features that would cause the app to be cluttered. I used to use another habit app… then they… added to-do list features. It just made the app unusable for me. Please don't try to be an all in one app!'; 'No-nonsense approach… without bloat. Plz keep it that way :)'; 'What you will not find here: being told which habit to do. Challenges against other people'; 'No plant that grows along, no timer you never use, just habit tracking'; 'Please keep the foundations of what you have created'; 'no gamification overload, no feeling that managing the habit tracker becomes a habit in itself'; 'kein Spam, keine Werbung, keine sinnlosen Tips'; 'Zero distractions, unlike other apps' — any roadmap must be read against it",
  "minimal, no gamification", "praise", "simplicity 338 (41.47%); design 284 (34.85%)", "product-rule", "high-priority", "yes",
  ["8414522828","9243307416","8238514048","8384484490","8584016453","14489261806","12395956072","13465174002"])
